  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_019, acc=0.639) uses ResNet50 as the image encoder in a multimodal setup. Image-only ResNet50 was very weak (0.208), yet adding it to RNA still improved performance (0.639 vs 0.591 RNA-only), suggesting the image modality contributes complementary but limited signal. The key uncertainty is whether a stronger image encoder (ImageNet ViT-L) can extract more useful features and further boost multimodal performance. Question tested: config_025 is a direct A/B comparison to config_019, changing only the image encoder from ResNet50 to ViT-L while keeping all other settings identical (multi-profile, PCA, avgpool, weighted fusion). This isolates the image encoder's contribution. Why best next: With a limited budget, a clean single-variable comparison to the current best maximizes information gain. If ViT-L improves performance, it identifies a clear exploitation path; if not, it confirms the image modality's ceiling and redirects effort toward RNA encoder improvements (scvi/scgpt) or other design choices."
}

